WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.302
Sam is a mythical and ancient deity whose origins may go back as far as 500 BCE,

00:00:04.356 --> 00:00:07.882
When the earliest Samhain celebrations took place in Celtic Ireland

00:00:07.946 --> 00:00:11.034
To celebrate the end of the harvest season and the beginning of the darker

00:00:11.082 --> 00:00:11.950
half of the year.

00:00:12.020 --> 00:00:14.826
During the gathering of the harvest, neighboring hillsides were illuminated

00:00:14.858 --> 00:00:18.106
with great bonfires, which families would use to light torches and ignite

00:00:18.138 --> 00:00:21.342
their own earth fires at home, which some sources believe were to continue

00:00:21.396 --> 00:00:23.406
burning until the harvest collection was complete.

00:00:23.508 --> 00:00:27.046
Their fires were said to keep away evil spirits, which was important because this

00:00:27.068 --> 00:00:29.522
festival called for ancient burial mounds to be opened.

00:00:29.586 --> 00:00:32.626
It was believed that these mounds were portals to The Other World, 

00:00:32.658 --> 00:00:35.362
a realm believed to contain Celtic deities and spirits of the dead.

00:00:35.426 --> 00:00:38.562
On Samhain, the veil between the living and the dead would be at its thinnest,

00:00:38.626 --> 00:00:40.758
allowing them to cross into the world of the living.

00:00:40.844 --> 00:00:44.138
With spirits and gods roaming free for an evening, a tradition was put in

00:00:44.144 --> 00:00:47.226
place to appease them with offerings of food and drinks in exchange for the

00:00:47.248 --> 00:00:49.302
survival of livestock over the coming winter.

00:00:49.366 --> 00:00:52.742
They also built altars to honor their dead ancestors, composed of elements

00:00:52.806 --> 00:00:56.218
from the natural world, like colorful leaves, burning candles, and symbols

00:00:56.234 --> 00:00:57.322
to commemorate the dead.

00:00:57.386 --> 00:01:00.158
They also used crops that were abundant in the fall, such as apples and

00:01:00.164 --> 00:01:03.674
pumpkins, to symbolize the harvest, and at some point, even placed skulls,

00:01:03.722 --> 00:01:07.586
skeletons, and images of deceased family members to symbolize and honor the dead.

00:01:07.608 --> 00:01:11.742
In Celtic folklore, a Sídhe was a fairy or flying supernatural entity.

00:01:11.806 --> 00:01:15.234
But these are a far cry from the pixie-like depiction of fairies often seen today.

00:01:15.272 --> 00:01:18.166
They were seen as troublemaking spirits, with some of the most

00:01:18.188 --> 00:01:21.746
popular examples of Irish fairies being Leprechauns, short fused mischievous little men;

00:01:21.778 --> 00:01:25.606
Banshees wailing female spirits with warnings of death; and

00:01:25.628 --> 00:01:29.446
Changelings, deformed unwanted children that other fairies would

00:01:29.468 --> 00:01:31.042
sometimes swap with human babies.

00:01:31.106 --> 00:01:34.378
The Irish word Sídhe literally translates to sudden blast of wind.

00:01:34.464 --> 00:01:37.910
So their fairies are really more akin to what we now think of as ghosts.

00:01:37.990 --> 00:01:40.890
Samhain was believed to be the time when these spirits could cross over.

00:01:40.960 --> 00:01:44.150
In particular, there were a few fairies associated with Samhain, like the

00:01:44.160 --> 00:01:47.326
Púca, a shapeshifting goblin that could take the appearance of animals or

00:01:47.348 --> 00:01:49.642
humans and bring either good or bad fortune.

00:01:49.706 --> 00:01:53.258
The Lady Gwyn was an evil headless woman wearing white luring journeymen

00:01:53.274 --> 00:01:53.914
into danger.

00:01:53.962 --> 00:01:57.326
The Dullahan was a malicious headless horseman, foreshadowing imminent death

00:01:57.358 --> 00:01:58.302
or misfortune.

00:01:58.366 --> 00:02:01.314
To protect themselves from this array of spirits, it became tradition to

00:02:01.352 --> 00:02:04.046
dress up as monsters to scare away the evil entities.

00:02:04.158 --> 00:02:07.422
This practice was known as Guising, you know, like disguising.

00:02:07.486 --> 00:02:11.074
In the 1500s, those wearing the costumes known as mummers,

00:02:11.122 --> 00:02:13.586
combined their traditions with another practice known as souling.

00:02:13.618 --> 00:02:16.946
from the Dark Ages. They would go door to door singing songs for the souls

00:02:16.978 --> 00:02:19.090
in purgatory in exchange for soul-cakes.

00:02:19.170 --> 00:02:22.906
Failure to participate in Samhain festivities was seen as taboo, and it was

00:02:22.928 --> 00:02:26.026
believed that those who did not take part would be punished by the gods with

00:02:26.048 --> 00:02:27.398
illness or even death.

00:02:27.494 --> 00:02:31.098
Celebrations began in the evening on October 31, the midpoint between the

00:02:31.104 --> 00:02:32.982
fall equinox and the winter solstice.

00:02:33.046 --> 00:02:36.158
As you may have figured out by now, this holiday eventually changed and

00:02:36.164 --> 00:02:39.626
morphed with other cultures over the years and became known as All Hollows Eve,

00:02:39.658 --> 00:02:41.738
or what we now know as Halloween.

00:02:41.834 --> 00:02:45.530
Altars for the dead became Halloween decorations. Hearth fires became Jack O’Lanterns.

00:02:45.540 --> 00:02:49.454
Mumming became Halloween costumes, and soul-cakes became Halloween candies.

00:02:49.502 --> 00:02:53.026
Punishment by the gods became punishment by toilet paper, and

00:02:53.048 --> 00:02:54.862
Guising became trick or treating.

00:02:54.926 --> 00:02:56.478
Which brings us back to Sam.

00:02:56.574 --> 00:03:00.198
As customs fused and evolved over the years, Sam's role was to uphold the

00:03:00.204 --> 00:03:01.362
traditions at their core.

00:03:01.426 --> 00:03:04.546
Even his name goes back to the ancient Celtic festival, which is spelled

00:03:04.578 --> 00:03:07.938
like this and sometimes mispronounced as Sam Hain.

00:03:08.034 --> 00:03:08.634
Thank you, Dr. Loomis.

00:03:08.672 --> 00:03:12.358
To learn how Sam became the ever present deity upholding the rules

00:03:12.374 --> 00:03:16.442
of Halloween set thousands of years ago, stick around to the end

00:03:16.496 --> 00:03:17.100
of this video.

00:03:17.100 --> 00:03:23.056
🎵Metal Music🎵

00:03:23.150 --> 00:03:24.586
Welcome to Horror History.

00:03:24.688 --> 00:03:27.726
This is a show where I analyze the timelines and lives of some of the most

00:03:27.748 --> 00:03:29.562
feared characters in the horror genre.

00:03:29.626 --> 00:03:33.534
But occasionally in horror history, we have to go back in actual history to

00:03:33.572 --> 00:03:35.130
understand a character's origins.

00:03:35.210 --> 00:03:38.366
However, I have to admit that is only partially the case today.

00:03:38.468 --> 00:03:42.206
While Samhain and fairies and banshees were all actually a part of the Irish

00:03:42.238 --> 00:03:46.034
folklore dating back thousands of years, Sam was not actually a part of that

00:03:46.072 --> 00:03:46.770
in real life.

00:03:46.840 --> 00:03:49.842
He wasn't even loosely based on a character from Irish folklore.

00:03:49.906 --> 00:03:53.014
While there are an array of deities, Samhain was not one of them.

00:03:53.052 --> 00:03:56.486
It was just the name of the festival literally translating to summer's end.

00:03:56.588 --> 00:03:59.954
Sam actually began as a doodling that writer director Michael Dougherty

00:04:00.002 --> 00:04:01.442
created in class when he was bored.

00:04:01.506 --> 00:04:04.714
The burlap sack over his head is meant to make him feel like a cross between

00:04:04.752 --> 00:04:05.942
a pumpkin and a scarecrow.

00:04:06.006 --> 00:04:09.466
Dougherty wanted the design to represent the holiday's dual nature:

00:04:09.488 --> 00:04:11.110
cute and creepy; fun and frightening;

00:04:11.190 --> 00:04:12.918
Mischievous yet malevolent.

00:04:13.014 --> 00:04:15.966
After making hundreds of drawings of the character, he decided he wanted to

00:04:15.988 --> 00:04:16.686
do something with it.

00:04:16.708 --> 00:04:19.946
So he spent nine months hand drawing the animated short film

00:04:19.978 --> 00:04:22.250
Season's Greetings as a senior thesis at NYU.

00:04:22.330 --> 00:04:25.246
Then the character was featured in actual greeting cards that he sent to

00:04:25.268 --> 00:04:28.306
friends and family, and eventually he sold the cards to a local shop in

00:04:28.328 --> 00:04:29.566
Burbank for distribution.

00:04:29.678 --> 00:04:33.326
Sam also found his way into other animated shorts such as Hellmark Cards in 2001.

00:04:33.358 --> 00:04:37.378
He also began to experiment with sketching Sam without the mask at

00:04:37.384 --> 00:04:37.890
this time.

00:04:37.960 --> 00:04:40.678
After showing the short film off around the industry, he was advised to

00:04:40.684 --> 00:04:43.202
write a feature length script as a vehicle for the character.

00:04:43.266 --> 00:04:46.486
So he combined three short stories he'd written as homework assignments in

00:04:46.508 --> 00:04:48.646
college to create the script for Trick r Treat.

00:04:48.748 --> 00:04:52.362
So Sam's association with the ancient Celtic culture is something that only

00:04:52.416 --> 00:04:53.622
exists in universe.

00:04:53.686 --> 00:04:57.302
But in a way, the rise in popularity of Trick r Treat through screenings,

00:04:57.366 --> 00:05:01.110
merchandising and fan artwork has cemented Sam as a Halloween icon.

00:05:01.190 --> 00:05:04.602
He's become an unofficial mascot of the holiday, and that was by design.

00:05:04.736 --> 00:05:08.606
Dougherty explains, I realize that while Christmas has Santa Claus, Easter had

00:05:08.628 --> 00:05:11.998
an egg laying rabbit, and Valentine's Day had chubby winged children that

00:05:12.004 --> 00:05:13.102
shot arrows at your heart.

00:05:13.156 --> 00:05:15.402
Halloween was missing a mythological mascot.

00:05:15.466 --> 00:05:17.022
I knew the character must be out there.

00:05:17.076 --> 00:05:18.110
He was just hiding.

00:05:18.190 --> 00:05:21.246
The image most commonly associated with Halloween is the Jack O Lantern,

00:05:21.278 --> 00:05:23.998
which is a practice derived from the Irish folktale of Stingy Jack.

00:05:24.014 --> 00:05:27.554
An old drunkard who tricked the devil into agreeing to never take his soul,

00:05:27.592 --> 00:05:30.886
leaving him to forever wander the plains between heaven and hell with

00:05:30.908 --> 00:05:33.670
only a light inside of a hollowed out turnip to light his way.

00:05:33.740 --> 00:05:37.234
That turnip eventually became a potato, which eventually became a pumpkin,

00:05:37.282 --> 00:05:39.298
which eventually became Jack Skellington.

00:05:39.394 --> 00:05:42.718
Sam continues the tradition as his uncovered head, seen at the end of

00:05:42.754 --> 00:05:45.846
Trick r treat, resembles a hollowed out pumpkin skull, and his body is filled

00:05:45.878 --> 00:05:46.790
with pumpkin guts.

00:05:46.870 --> 00:05:50.026
While Dougherty has stated that he'll never reveal Sam's true origins, there

00:05:50.048 --> 00:05:53.594
is an extensive history to unpack in the comics, the movie, and many short

00:05:53.632 --> 00:05:55.262
films that the character has appeared in.

00:05:55.316 --> 00:05:58.906
So to fully understand the motivations to this mysterious malevolent munchkin,

00:05:58.938 --> 00:06:01.354
we've got to take it all the way back to Ireland

00:06:01.402 --> 00:06:03.630
In the mid 1600s.

00:06:03.630 --> 00:06:04.383
(Impact)

00:06:04.383 --> 00:06:08.511
🎵Mysterious Music🎵

00:06:08.630 --> 00:06:13.586
On October 24, 1640, a man named Thomas is criticized for showing mercy on

00:06:13.608 --> 00:06:15.038
witches during their execution.

00:06:15.134 --> 00:06:18.338
The man in charge of the executions, Commander Wolfric, explains that the

00:06:18.344 --> 00:06:21.494
harvest season is ending and the pagan witches will soon be at their full power.

00:06:21.532 --> 00:06:24.598
He sends Thomas to the interrogation tents to toughen him up, where

00:06:24.604 --> 00:06:26.818
he rescues a suspected witch named Brigid.

00:06:26.914 --> 00:06:30.482
She explains that what Thomas's people perceived as a devil worship ritual

00:06:30.546 --> 00:06:32.982
was actually an act to honor the spirits of the dead.

00:06:33.046 --> 00:06:36.074
We believe it's the one night when they're permitted to return, so we light

00:06:36.112 --> 00:06:37.754
candles and bonfires to guide them.

00:06:37.792 --> 00:06:41.626
We offer crops as gifts and dress in guises to protect them and us from the

00:06:41.648 --> 00:06:43.450
truly dark forces that prowl the night.

00:06:43.520 --> 00:06:46.954
She clarifies that they believe all life is sacred and uncovers a seed

00:06:47.002 --> 00:06:50.206
hidden away under a specific rock, claiming it contains the last of her

00:06:50.228 --> 00:06:51.050
people's magic.

00:06:51.130 --> 00:06:55.006
As days and nights pass, Thomas is unable to see the devil in her eyes, and

00:06:55.028 --> 00:06:58.202
Sam can be seen observing Thomas's internal struggle from afar.

00:06:58.266 --> 00:07:01.966
On October 30, Brigid is tortured by some of the other soldiers and uses

00:07:01.998 --> 00:07:05.118
her magic to break free and grow pumpkin vines, which are able to shape

00:07:05.134 --> 00:07:06.658
themselves to unlock her cell.

00:07:06.744 --> 00:07:10.546
Instead of escaping, she finds Thomas, who has grown sick and uses her vine

00:07:10.578 --> 00:07:13.718
magic to cure him, while simultaneously giving him a vision of the

00:07:13.724 --> 00:07:16.050
slaughtering of her people by the Christian soldiers.

00:07:16.130 --> 00:07:18.070
Her execution is set for the next night,

00:07:18.140 --> 00:07:19.414
October 31st, Samhain.

00:07:19.532 --> 00:07:22.886
Thomas attempts to rescue her, but they're captured by Commander

00:07:22.918 --> 00:07:26.506
Wolfric, and as they're being burned at the stake, Brigid sees Sam, his

00:07:26.528 --> 00:07:29.274
eyes glowing in a clearing, and believes that her prayers have been answered. 

00:07:29.312 --> 00:07:33.242
Wolfric smashes her magic pumpkin, but the next day, a young girl

00:07:33.296 --> 00:07:35.774
discovers it, collects the seeds, and brings them with her during her

00:07:35.812 --> 00:07:39.246
eventual journey to the New World. Thomas and Brigid go on as spirits,

00:07:39.268 --> 00:07:42.654
and Sam's face can be seen in the blood moon that supposedly gives

00:07:42.692 --> 00:07:44.282
power to their pagan cults.

00:07:44.346 --> 00:07:47.794
Sam's role in the story is essentially a protector of the Samhain magic that

00:07:47.832 --> 00:07:49.394
allows the supernatural to come to life on October 31st.

00:07:49.432 --> 00:07:53.234
Thomas and Brigid are forbidden lovers, whose relationship

00:07:53.352 --> 00:07:56.654
represents the cultural diffusion that occurred to combine the pagan holiday

00:07:56.702 --> 00:08:00.566
of Samhain with the Christian holiday of All Saints Day to create Halloween.

00:08:00.588 --> 00:08:02.406
As it is celebrated in the west today.

00:08:02.508 --> 00:08:06.114
We literally see their seed go on without them to the New World, where Sam

00:08:06.162 --> 00:08:09.242
would continue to watch over it for autumn celebrations across many

00:08:09.296 --> 00:08:13.210
different cultures, the next of which would be in the wild, wild west.

00:08:13.210 --> 00:08:15.795
(Impact)

00:08:18.001 --> 00:08:22.690
🎵Folk Music🎵

00:08:22.690 --> 00:08:24.990
Illinois. October 29th, 1853.

00:08:25.060 --> 00:08:27.994
European settlers have brought their Halloween traditions to the Americas

00:08:28.042 --> 00:08:30.766
and are actively spreading further west through the construction of a

00:08:30.788 --> 00:08:32.170
transcontinental railroad.

00:08:32.250 --> 00:08:35.294
When we first meet our main character of this story, Sarah, she's even

00:08:35.332 --> 00:08:38.686
reading The Legend of Sleepy Hollow, the tale of a man haunted by a headless

00:08:38.718 --> 00:08:42.286
horseman, a direct connection back to the Celtic fairy, the Dullahan, proving

00:08:42.318 --> 00:08:45.710
that the Halloween she celebrates has a direct connection back to Ireland.

00:08:45.790 --> 00:08:48.414
But they are not the only ones celebrating the falling leaves.

00:08:48.462 --> 00:08:51.794
Sarah's father discovers a Native American tribe blocking his potential

00:08:51.842 --> 00:08:52.482
train route.

00:08:52.546 --> 00:08:55.906
Sarah befriends a native girl named P’wani who teaches her about her tribe's

00:08:55.938 --> 00:08:59.362
shaman praying to the corn maiden as thanks for their bountiful harvest.

00:08:59.426 --> 00:09:03.078
They discuss good and evil spirits, so P’wani gives her a small cornstalk

00:09:03.094 --> 00:09:03.910
version of Sam.

00:09:03.990 --> 00:09:07.014
Even though the tribe does not know what Halloween is, they still recognize Sam,

00:09:07.062 --> 00:09:10.518
which tells us that Sam is a deity who watches over all autumnal

00:09:10.534 --> 00:09:13.914
festivals from a variety of cultures, not just those directly derived from Samhain.

00:09:13.952 --> 00:09:17.806
Sarah asks if he's a good spirit, and P’wani tells her, I would not say that,

00:09:17.828 --> 00:09:21.546
but the shaman told me he is very old and very powerful.

00:09:21.658 --> 00:09:24.766
Sarah carries her Sam doll with her as she tries to convince her father to

00:09:24.788 --> 00:09:26.606
leave the natives alone, to no avail.

00:09:26.708 --> 00:09:29.986
In the night, she sees the corn maiden and follows her shadow back to the tribe,

00:09:30.008 --> 00:09:32.962
where she's informed that the maiden was once a human whose touch

00:09:33.016 --> 00:09:34.494
brought life to the crop fields.

00:09:34.542 --> 00:09:37.874
But when the gold seekers arrived, they feared her magic and killed her.

00:09:37.912 --> 00:09:40.530
But even when her blood fell, fertile crops arose.

00:09:40.610 --> 00:09:43.574
They celebrate the autumn harvest to honor the corn maiden and teach

00:09:43.612 --> 00:09:46.278
children of the dangers that lurk in the dark hearts of man.

00:09:46.364 --> 00:09:49.426
Sarah tells of her own Halloween traditions, and they agree to celebrate together.

00:09:49.458 --> 00:09:50.710
The next morning

00:09:50.780 --> 00:09:53.706
She even gets the unexpected blessing from her father, who sends her with candy.

00:09:53.728 --> 00:09:57.206
Sarah crafts her own Sam O'Lantern to protect them from the evil spirts,

00:09:57.238 --> 00:10:00.106
but soon discovers that the candy her father sent with her was

00:10:00.128 --> 00:10:03.334
poisoned as a covert attack by her father looking to clear out the Indian settlement.

00:10:03.382 --> 00:10:07.562
Sam, or as she knows him, the great autumn spirit, takes notice,

00:10:07.626 --> 00:10:10.606
follows her to the shaman's Cauldron, and seemingly grants her the power of

00:10:10.628 --> 00:10:13.914
the corn maiden, giving her the magic ability to take revenge on her father

00:10:13.962 --> 00:10:17.314
and his friends, vitriolically growing vines out of their intestines before

00:10:17.352 --> 00:10:18.126
appearing in the fog

00:10:18.158 --> 00:10:22.290
With Sam at her side and annihilating her death. She takes Sam's hand before

00:10:22.360 --> 00:10:25.566
disappearing back into the corn with the only evidence left behind a patch

00:10:25.598 --> 00:10:26.174
of pumpkins

00:10:26.222 --> 00:10:28.930
With the settler's shocked faces imprinted upon them.

00:10:29.000 --> 00:10:32.354
In this story, Sam demonstrates how the old tradition of guising and souling

00:10:32.402 --> 00:10:35.522
must be honored even as it takes a different form on a new continent.

00:10:35.586 --> 00:10:38.034
The deal is to offer sweets in exchange for culture.

00:10:38.082 --> 00:10:41.394
The tribe shares their culture with Sarah and, by extension, the settlers.

00:10:41.442 --> 00:10:44.698
But the railroad men violate the deal by poisoning the candy given in return.

00:10:44.704 --> 00:10:48.138
And this is not the last time we would see Sam act on a situation

00:10:48.224 --> 00:10:48.810
like this.

00:10:48.880 --> 00:10:49.626
But first.

00:10:49.728 --> 00:10:52.906
Los Angeles, October 30, 1955.

00:10:53.008 --> 00:10:56.394
Jake Perkins is a private investigator without any interest in celebrating Halloween.

00:10:56.442 --> 00:10:59.918
One day, a woman hires him to find her missing sister, who may

00:10:59.924 --> 00:11:03.050
have been involved with a cult leader known as the Echo Park Devil.

00:11:03.130 --> 00:11:06.746
His search eventually takes him to a movie producer named T.E. Knickerbocker,

00:11:06.778 --> 00:11:09.778
who, by the way, is named after the Knickerbocker Hotel in Hollywood, which

00:11:09.784 --> 00:11:11.458
has housed many stars over the years.

00:11:11.544 --> 00:11:14.846
Anyway, when he arrives and peeks through the window, he sees a ritualistic

00:11:14.878 --> 00:11:18.526
costume party with many monsters gathered around a pumpkin resembling Sam's head.

00:11:18.558 --> 00:11:21.174
Thinking Jake is the killer, they kidnap him.

00:11:21.212 --> 00:11:24.086
But once he clears his name, he finds out that they were all performing a

00:11:24.108 --> 00:11:27.842
ritual to honor their fallen sisters, the victims of the Echo Park Devil.

00:11:27.906 --> 00:11:31.314
Like the pagans in the first story, they too, are just misunderstood,

00:11:31.362 --> 00:11:35.158
innocents celebrating nature, the spirits, and the cycle of life and death.

00:11:35.254 --> 00:11:38.358
They've been praying for an avenging angel to finally defeat the Echo Park Devil,

00:11:38.374 --> 00:11:41.754
and they believe that that person is none other than Jake, chosen by

00:11:41.792 --> 00:11:44.538
forces much older and wiser than either of them.

00:11:44.624 --> 00:11:48.314
That force appears to be Sam, so Jake relents and searches an abandoned

00:11:48.362 --> 00:11:51.562
church, where he finds the missing girl just as he's ambushed by the devil.

00:11:51.626 --> 00:11:54.666
The chase leads them to the rooftop, where, after a tough battle, the devil

00:11:54.698 --> 00:11:57.886
is thrown off the building, and he's eventually unmasked to reveal the mayor

00:11:57.918 --> 00:12:01.426
of the city, the one capitalizing on all of the fear about the killer in his

00:12:01.448 --> 00:12:02.558
reelection campaign.

00:12:02.654 --> 00:12:05.826
As if things weren't strange enough, the missing woman was revealed to have

00:12:05.848 --> 00:12:09.266
been dead all along, and she did not even have a sister, implying that it

00:12:09.288 --> 00:12:11.622
was actually her ghost who hired Jake onto the case.

00:12:11.676 --> 00:12:15.986
With Sam seemingly pulling the strings, it ends with Jake now with no choice

00:12:16.018 --> 00:12:17.922
but to be a believer in the supernatural.

00:12:17.986 --> 00:12:21.046
In this one, Sam protects the Halloween tradition in multiple ways.

00:12:21.148 --> 00:12:24.518
Non participants have long said to be punished by the gods, and Jake's lack

00:12:24.534 --> 00:12:27.866
of Halloween spirit is because he believes that dead is dead and gone is gone.

00:12:27.888 --> 00:12:30.042
He doesn't believe that any of it is real.

00:12:30.096 --> 00:12:32.330
He's also taught to honor the dead throughout the story.

00:12:32.400 --> 00:12:35.994
It is only after finally visiting his deceased wife and son in the graveyard

00:12:36.042 --> 00:12:38.602
when he realizes where the Echo Park Devil is hiding.

00:12:38.666 --> 00:12:42.062
The last story of the Days of the Dead comic takes place about 50 years

00:12:42.116 --> 00:12:44.990
before modern day, most likely the mid 1960s.

00:12:45.060 --> 00:12:48.318
James and Rory are a pair of troublemaking kids who get caught vandalizing

00:12:48.334 --> 00:12:49.570
houses on Halloween night.

00:12:49.640 --> 00:12:51.582
Rory is the son of the reverend at the church.

00:12:51.646 --> 00:12:54.606
As they're being punished, they're all surrounded by a horde of classic

00:12:54.638 --> 00:12:57.950
monsters, including werewolves, witches, vampires, and demons.

00:12:58.030 --> 00:13:01.334
While the adults are scared away, james and Rory put their mask back on,

00:13:01.372 --> 00:13:03.730
allowing them to blend in with the monsters undetected.

00:13:03.810 --> 00:13:07.478
That is, until the Grim Reaper appears before them and they wake up under an

00:13:07.484 --> 00:13:10.866
apple tree in the midst of an awesome Halloween party put on by the monsters

00:13:10.898 --> 00:13:12.330
and decide to celebrate with them.

00:13:12.400 --> 00:13:15.254
Judging by their hands, they seem to be slowly turning into monsters themselves,

00:13:15.302 --> 00:13:18.534
and they join the crowd as everyone gathers around the leader,

00:13:18.582 --> 00:13:19.830
which, of course, is Sam.

00:13:19.910 --> 00:13:23.226
He throws a handful of candy into the fire, causing it to shoot skyward, and

00:13:23.248 --> 00:13:25.002
some of the monsters fly up after it.

00:13:25.056 --> 00:13:28.026
James and Rory spend the night riding around with the monsters, dispersing

00:13:28.058 --> 00:13:31.406
candy to kids all over town, ending at the church, where their community is

00:13:31.428 --> 00:13:34.206
holding a lock in designed to prevent them from doing anything fun on Halloween.

00:13:34.228 --> 00:13:37.506
The monsters break their way in, and the boys join them in

00:13:37.528 --> 00:13:38.958
terrorizing the congregation.

00:13:39.054 --> 00:13:42.226
When the reverend spots Rory, he tells him, I always knew there was

00:13:42.248 --> 00:13:43.170
something wrong with you.

00:13:43.240 --> 00:13:46.882
Rory attacks him, claiming he'd rather be like a monster than be like him.

00:13:46.936 --> 00:13:50.694
But just then, the clock strikes midnight, and the monsters disappear into

00:13:50.732 --> 00:13:51.232
the night.

00:13:51.260 --> 00:13:54.562
James urges them to take their masks off before it's too late, but Rory

00:13:54.626 --> 00:13:58.246
claims that this is where he belongs, and the Grim Reaper fully turns him

00:13:58.268 --> 00:14:01.862
into a monster before taking off and leaving his best friend behind.

00:14:01.996 --> 00:14:05.146
We then jump forward to basically the present day, where James has just

00:14:05.168 --> 00:14:08.138
finished telling his granddaughter each of these four Halloween tales, and

00:14:08.144 --> 00:14:10.026
she runs off to trick or treat with her friends.

00:14:10.128 --> 00:14:13.030
Only one of them turns back, and it's Sam.

00:14:13.110 --> 00:14:17.086
He looks up and sees Rory in his monstrous form flying over the moon before

00:14:17.108 --> 00:14:18.682
he's greeted by the Grim Reaper.

00:14:18.746 --> 00:14:19.582
And that's it.

00:14:19.636 --> 00:14:21.390
We don't find out what happened after that.

00:14:21.460 --> 00:14:24.650
I think Sam's purpose in this story is to be the catalyst for mischief.

00:14:24.730 --> 00:14:28.046
According to English historian Ronald Hutton, when imitating malignant spirits,

00:14:28.078 --> 00:14:31.182
it was a very short step from guising to playing pranks.

00:14:31.246 --> 00:14:34.466
Samhain pranks became common in Ireland and Scotland, leading Samhain to be

00:14:34.488 --> 00:14:36.894
known as Mischief Night in parts of those countries.

00:14:37.022 --> 00:14:39.498
Remember, Sam is neither a good or evil spirit.

00:14:39.534 --> 00:14:42.914
He is simply an embodiment of all things Halloween and Samhain.

00:14:42.962 --> 00:14:45.874
It's also significant that these pranks came at the expense of the church,

00:14:45.922 --> 00:14:49.014
because while most Christian churches have come to accept Halloween, some

00:14:49.052 --> 00:14:51.746
very religious groups still object to its celebration.

00:14:51.858 --> 00:14:55.146
Also, this present timeline with James and his granddaughter is not given a

00:14:55.168 --> 00:14:55.898
specific date.

00:14:55.984 --> 00:14:59.178
It's more or less modern day, along with each of the short films and,

00:14:59.184 --> 00:15:02.714
Of course, the movie, which all seem like they could be set in the 2000s.

00:15:02.752 --> 00:15:05.074
A time when cell phones and rotary phones still coexisted.

00:15:05.142 --> 00:15:08.526
The movie does feature a werewolf transformation, so if we're going by real

00:15:08.548 --> 00:15:11.406
world calendars, the nearest full moon on Halloween would have been in

00:15:11.428 --> 00:15:12.754
October 2001.

00:15:12.792 --> 00:15:16.386
However, the movie also features a flashback, allowing us to jump back in

00:15:16.408 --> 00:15:19.220
time and catch Sam in a period bygone. 

00:15:19.220 --> 00:15:22.248
(Impact)

00:15:24.276 --> 00:15:28.137
🎵Mysterious Music🎵 

00:15:28.230 --> 00:15:30.482
Thirty years before the events of Trick r Treat,

00:15:30.546 --> 00:15:34.402
So most likely sometime in the 1970s, a school bus carrying eight troubled,

00:15:34.466 --> 00:15:38.006
disturbed kids from Happy Shepherd Academy went off its usual route on Halloween.

00:15:38.028 --> 00:15:41.826
and past a pumpkin patch where Sam can be seen prodding at a dead

00:15:41.858 --> 00:15:42.894
crow with a stick.

00:15:42.962 --> 00:15:44.822
The bus stopped before the quarry's edge.

00:15:44.886 --> 00:15:48.266
The driver had been hired by the children's exhausted parents to dispose of them,

00:15:48.288 --> 00:15:51.354
but when he got up to check on their chains, one of the students got

00:15:51.392 --> 00:15:53.750
free and sent the bus barreling off the cliff.

00:15:53.830 --> 00:15:56.766
Based on the ancient legends of the spirits of the dead roaming free on

00:15:56.788 --> 00:16:00.782
Halloween, Sam did not necessarily have to intervene in order for these kids

00:16:00.836 --> 00:16:03.406
ghosts to haunt the area every October 31st.

00:16:03.508 --> 00:16:06.702
In this instance, Sam is just a bystander with an interest in all things morbid,

00:16:06.756 --> 00:16:09.678
but his next appearance would be less passive.

00:16:09.774 --> 00:16:13.346
In Seasons Greeting, Sam appears as a trick or treater, and a man follows him

00:16:13.368 --> 00:16:15.026
into an alley and tries to beat him up.

00:16:15.048 --> 00:16:18.786
But Sam destroys him and carries him away in his sack before revealing his

00:16:18.808 --> 00:16:20.238
true supernatural nature.

00:16:20.334 --> 00:16:23.478
Obviously, the lesson here is that you don't with Sam, and it's important to

00:16:23.484 --> 00:16:24.870
keep context in mind, too.

00:16:24.940 --> 00:16:27.858
This was the first thing he ever appeared in, so viewers would have assumed

00:16:27.874 --> 00:16:30.790
that he was just a kid in a Halloween costume... until the end.

00:16:30.860 --> 00:16:34.022
To a bystander, Sam appears to just be a kid in a strange costume.

00:16:34.086 --> 00:16:37.786
In fact, director Mike Dougherty insisted on it being an actual child in the

00:16:37.808 --> 00:16:40.214
costume to ensure that the body language would be authentic.

00:16:40.262 --> 00:16:43.466
Which ties into the desire to make Sam represent both the fun side of

00:16:43.488 --> 00:16:44.990
Halloween and the scary side.

00:16:45.060 --> 00:16:48.250
Charlie Corrigan was a portly child of 180 pounds.

00:16:48.330 --> 00:16:51.498
According to the book, he typically spent Halloween terrorizing the mites

00:16:51.514 --> 00:16:54.686
who took the time to dress up, stealing their candy and amassing a horde as

00:16:54.708 --> 00:16:55.550
the night went on.

00:16:55.620 --> 00:16:58.322
Given this arrangement, he didn't have much need to dress up.

00:16:58.376 --> 00:17:01.794
Why bother if you could just take all the candy you wanted?

00:17:01.832 --> 00:17:04.786
Well, maybe one reason is disguising yourself from getting caught which is what happens

00:17:04.808 --> 00:17:08.126
when his principal, Steven Wilkins, sees him in the act of taking more than one piece.

00:17:08.168 --> 00:17:11.654
Wilkins gets the boy's guard down by offering him more candy which

00:17:11.692 --> 00:17:13.030
makes Charlie violently ill.

00:17:13.100 --> 00:17:16.566
This candy has been laced with hydrofluoric acid, causing Charlie to

00:17:16.588 --> 00:17:19.586
projectile vomit a reference to one of Mike Dougherty's favorite horror

00:17:19.618 --> 00:17:20.738
movies, The Exorcist.

00:17:20.834 --> 00:17:24.406
After lugging Charlie's massive body inside three other students come

00:17:24.438 --> 00:17:27.338
Trick or treating at Principal Wilkins' door asking to have one of his

00:17:27.344 --> 00:17:29.828
jack o lanterns which he allows them to get them to leave him alone. 

00:17:29.828 --> 00:17:30.992
We'll come back to them,

00:17:30.992 --> 00:17:33.430
But as they exit, he notices a fourth figure.

00:17:33.520 --> 00:17:36.602
It's Sam, who says nothing as he hastily takes his candy.

00:17:36.666 --> 00:17:38.190
Wilkins has passed this test.

00:17:38.260 --> 00:17:41.182
There's no Halloween rule about kidnapping an obese boy,

00:17:41.236 --> 00:17:41.736
I guess.

00:17:41.780 --> 00:17:44.510
As Sam walks away, pay attention to his bag.

00:17:46.610 --> 00:17:48.714
It sounds like there's a live cat in his sack.

00:17:48.762 --> 00:17:51.450
A possible reference to the original old sketches of Sam.

00:17:51.530 --> 00:17:54.746
Wilkins buries Charlie in the backyard drawing annoyance from his next door

00:17:54.778 --> 00:17:55.414
neighbor were Mr. Krieg,

00:17:55.452 --> 00:17:59.186
but not before decapitating him and using the head as a jack o lantern

00:17:59.218 --> 00:18:01.606
that he carves with his son in the basement later that night.

00:18:01.708 --> 00:18:04.918
Since there's no rule about what you can use as a template for your jack o lantern

00:18:04.924 --> 00:18:08.118
remember, the original jack o lanterns were made from turnips and potatoes.

00:18:08.124 --> 00:18:11.042
This also doesn't get him in any trouble with Sam.

00:18:11.106 --> 00:18:13.818
However, he would run into other issues later that night.

00:18:13.904 --> 00:18:17.274
He puts on a vampire costume for his date that evening who he ends up making

00:18:17.312 --> 00:18:19.494
out with in an alley next to the Halloween parade.

00:18:19.542 --> 00:18:22.954
Though his fangs are fake, his bite is real and he draws blood from the girl

00:18:22.992 --> 00:18:26.138
whose pleas are ignored because everyone assumes that it's costume blood.

00:18:26.234 --> 00:18:29.454
Jumping back to the beginning of the night, Lauri, her sister and their friends

00:18:29.492 --> 00:18:32.666
are a group of girls visiting Warren Valley, Ohio for their yearly

00:18:32.698 --> 00:18:33.722
Halloween boy hunt.

00:18:33.786 --> 00:18:37.106
And when I say hunt, I mean that literally because although we don't know it

00:18:37.128 --> 00:18:39.214
yet, these girls have lycanthropy.

00:18:39.262 --> 00:18:40.238
They're werewolves.

00:18:40.334 --> 00:18:43.058
-[Laurie] I don't know why we drove out here when there are perfectly good guys in the city.

00:18:43.064 --> 00:18:44.142
-[Janet] Fresh meat.

00:18:44.206 --> 00:18:46.786
They choose a different city for their ritual each year.

00:18:46.888 --> 00:18:48.210
-[Danielle] Tampa was two years ago.

00:18:48.280 --> 00:18:49.646
-[Danielle] I remember because you puked while doing a guy in the back of his pickup. 

00:18:49.678 --> 00:18:54.006
-[Janet] I ate some bad Mexican, and it was a Jeep. 

00:18:54.108 --> 00:18:56.278
Notice how she didn't say Mexican food.

00:18:56.364 --> 00:18:59.574
The girls each go as fairytale characters, with Laurie dressed up as

00:18:59.612 --> 00:19:00.194
Red Riding Hood.

00:19:00.242 --> 00:19:02.678
They set out to find dates for the party that they're going to, and the

00:19:02.684 --> 00:19:05.010
girls try to give her advice about losing her virginity.

00:19:05.090 --> 00:19:08.162
She goes off on her own for a while to try to meet someone, but eventually

00:19:08.226 --> 00:19:10.958
finds that someone has a sinister eye on her.

00:19:11.044 --> 00:19:14.526
It's Steven Wilkins again, still dressed in the same vampire attire from

00:19:14.548 --> 00:19:15.530
earlier in the evening.

00:19:15.610 --> 00:19:18.846
He follows her through the woods later that night, sneaks up behind her and grabs her. 

00:19:18.868 --> 00:19:19.840
-[Steven] My my, what big eyes you have. 

00:19:25.810 --> 00:19:28.702
Only Laurie puts a twist on the classic tale.

00:19:28.766 --> 00:19:32.354
In the original Red Riding Hood fable, a wolf disguises himself as

00:19:32.392 --> 00:19:34.514
Red Riding Hood's grandmother and tries to eat her.

00:19:34.552 --> 00:19:38.286
But in this case, Red Riding Hood herself is the wolf and the predator.

00:19:38.398 --> 00:19:41.766
She tosses Wilkins into the party wrapped in her cloak, then emerges from

00:19:41.788 --> 00:19:43.218
the woods in a new costume.

00:19:43.314 --> 00:19:46.658
After explaining what happened to her sister, she informs Wilkins that it's

00:19:46.674 --> 00:19:50.074
her first time and begins her transformation into wolf as she tears him

00:19:50.112 --> 00:19:51.450
apart with her teeth.

00:19:54.830 --> 00:19:57.030
Sam watches this ritual intensely.

00:19:57.110 --> 00:20:00.566
It's also significant that Wilkins goes out as a vampire because vampires

00:20:00.598 --> 00:20:02.262
and werewolves are known to be rivals.

00:20:02.326 --> 00:20:04.762
It seems to stem from the old Universal monster vs. movies,

00:20:04.826 --> 00:20:08.266
and maybe the fact that vampires avoid the sun while werewolves lose

00:20:08.298 --> 00:20:09.482
control at a full moon.

00:20:09.546 --> 00:20:12.926
The popcorn affair between these two supernatural races doesn't seem to have

00:20:12.948 --> 00:20:16.126
any ties to the ancient traditions of Samhain, but it is possible that this

00:20:16.148 --> 00:20:18.782
is a newer tradition that Sam seems to be embracing.

00:20:18.846 --> 00:20:21.886
The transformation itself was shot to stand out from traditional werewolf

00:20:21.918 --> 00:20:23.230
transformation scenes in movies.

00:20:23.310 --> 00:20:26.606
In Tales of Mayhem, Mystery and Mischief, collaborator Brian Singer

00:20:26.638 --> 00:20:29.894
explained how Doherty wanted it to look like a sensual experience rather

00:20:29.932 --> 00:20:31.894
than an excruciating hatching process.

00:20:32.012 --> 00:20:35.414
The werewolves transform in a kind of Dance of the Seven Veils, where they

00:20:35.452 --> 00:20:37.298
strip down to their true forms.

00:20:37.394 --> 00:20:40.578
There's also a great emphasis on the fact that Laurie is a virgin, which turns

00:20:40.594 --> 00:20:42.614
out to be a word that they're using connotatively.

00:20:42.662 --> 00:20:44.774
They're referring to her first time devouring a victim.

00:20:44.822 --> 00:20:47.258
But the allegory for sex is obviously still there.

00:20:47.344 --> 00:20:51.066
If my thesis that Sam is meant to embody Halloween and its traditions is correct,

00:20:51.088 --> 00:20:53.974
then I see no reason that that couldn't include more recent traditions,

00:20:54.022 --> 00:20:56.958
like the one where many young women use their costumes as a

00:20:56.964 --> 00:20:59.342
means to draw romantic attention to themselves.

00:20:59.476 --> 00:21:02.654
In recent decades, the holiday has taken a page from horror movies to become

00:21:02.692 --> 00:21:04.538
something both sexy and scary.

00:21:04.634 --> 00:21:08.446
But when you're a kid, hopefully, the focus on Halloween is more about fear

00:21:08.478 --> 00:21:09.214
and mischief.

00:21:09.262 --> 00:21:11.426
So let's go back to the beginning of the night once more.

00:21:11.528 --> 00:21:14.914
After collecting a carved pumpkin from Principal Wilkins house, 13 year old

00:21:14.952 --> 00:21:16.798
Chip, Macy and Sara hit up

00:21:16.814 --> 00:21:18.386
Mrs. Henderson's house, looking for another.

00:21:18.488 --> 00:21:21.894
Here we literally see how Halloween is celebrated differently as you get older.

00:21:21.932 --> 00:21:24.674
The three are joined by Schrader, who has collected an additional

00:21:24.722 --> 00:21:25.842
three jack o lanterns.

00:21:25.906 --> 00:21:28.994
Then they come across the jackpot of all jack o lanterns in the front yard of Rhonda,

00:21:29.042 --> 00:21:32.866
who they refer to as an idiot savant, someone with high aptitude

00:21:32.898 --> 00:21:36.050
in one subject, but reduced intellectual or social functioning.

00:21:36.130 --> 00:21:39.154
They all head out to the quarry, where Rhonda demonstrates her extensive

00:21:39.202 --> 00:21:40.650
knowledge of Samhain to Chip.

00:21:40.730 --> 00:21:43.358
Upon arriving, Macy says that they're going to pay their respects to the

00:21:43.364 --> 00:21:45.518
dead and tells the story of the crashed school bus.

00:21:45.604 --> 00:21:48.954
Each of the 8th jack o lanterns they've collected represents one of the lost

00:21:49.002 --> 00:21:50.174
souls from the school.

00:21:50.292 --> 00:21:53.486
We're going to leave them by the side of the lake as an offering to those

00:21:53.508 --> 00:21:54.042
who died.

00:21:54.106 --> 00:21:57.618
The mining elevator used to descend into the quarry can only hold three at a

00:21:57.624 --> 00:22:00.190
time, so Rhonda and Chip have to wait for the second trip.

00:22:00.270 --> 00:22:03.826
They hear blood curdling screams from their classmates below, and when they

00:22:03.848 --> 00:22:07.586
reach the bottom, chip acts as if he's too scared to go on, leading Rhonda

00:22:07.618 --> 00:22:11.151
to venture forward and look for the others in the dark, all on her own.

00:22:11.434 --> 00:22:13.893
(Impact)

00:22:16.391 --> 00:22:20.250
🎵Mysterious Music🎵 

00:22:20.250 --> 00:22:24.186
Rhonda roves through the thick fog in search of her lost classmates, and she

00:22:24.208 --> 00:22:26.026
comes across the deserted school bus.

00:22:26.128 --> 00:22:29.514
With no sign of the others in the vicinity, she's suddenly grabbed by what

00:22:29.552 --> 00:22:30.870
appears to be a pair of zombies.

00:22:30.950 --> 00:22:33.974
She runs for it and finds Chip lying on the ground with another zombie

00:22:34.022 --> 00:22:36.570
standing over him, intestines dangling from its mouth.

00:22:36.650 --> 00:22:40.078
They all give chase, and in a moment of panic, Rhonda slips and hits her

00:22:40.084 --> 00:22:42.222
head on a rock, she's knocked out.

00:22:42.276 --> 00:22:46.014
And when she awakes in tears, she learns that it had all been a cruel prank

00:22:46.062 --> 00:22:47.278
orchestrated by Macy.

00:22:47.374 --> 00:22:51.138
As they get ready to leave, Macy kicks the last nearby jack o lantern into the lake,

00:22:51.144 --> 00:22:54.350
extinguishing their final means of protection against the spirits.

00:22:54.430 --> 00:22:58.046
They are surrounded by ghostly voices, and before long see the ghastly

00:22:58.078 --> 00:23:00.502
silhouettes of the dead schoolchildren surrounding them.

00:23:00.556 --> 00:23:04.194
As they try to escape, Sarah is pulled away into the abyss, and Chip, Macy, and Schrader

00:23:04.242 --> 00:23:07.654
continue onto the elevator, where they find Rhonda locked behind

00:23:07.692 --> 00:23:09.714
the gate with the only remaining jack o lantern.

00:23:09.762 --> 00:23:13.238
But with her sympathy towards her spiteful classmates long since expired,

00:23:13.334 --> 00:23:16.138
presses the button and returns to safety without them.

00:23:16.224 --> 00:23:20.438
As their final screams emanate from the quarry below, Rhonda sees Sam hiding

00:23:20.454 --> 00:23:24.638
in a pipe, and they have a moment of eye contact, or in her case, I guess,

00:23:24.724 --> 00:23:25.662
sack contact.

00:23:25.796 --> 00:23:28.590
That sounds kind of wrong, but each of them continues on their way.

00:23:28.660 --> 00:23:32.046
The book specifically describes this interaction from Sam as a nod of approval.

00:23:32.068 --> 00:23:35.034
Something I found interesting was that Rhonda is wearing a witch costume throughout the story.

00:23:35.082 --> 00:23:38.306
Samhain was first observed by pagans in Ireland

00:23:38.328 --> 00:23:42.258
and paganism has long been tied to witchcraft. Jumping back to the middle of the evening,

00:23:42.264 --> 00:23:45.646
Old Man Krieg is the older version of the bus driver

00:23:45.678 --> 00:23:49.074
from Happy Shepherd Academy and the legend of the quarry crash from 30 years ago.

00:23:49.112 --> 00:23:52.774
He's now a grumpy dude living in a dark house with his dog scaring away

00:23:52.812 --> 00:23:56.198
trick or treaters and stealing their dropped candy. Dougherty describes him in

00:23:56.204 --> 00:23:59.938
the book as a Scrooge-esque man tormented for not celebrating Halloween's

00:23:59.954 --> 00:24:00.930
strict customs.

00:24:01.010 --> 00:24:04.234
I think an argument should be made that he's actually celebrating in his own way.

00:24:04.272 --> 00:24:07.786
Although he has no decorations, there's still a spooky ambiance, and

00:24:07.808 --> 00:24:09.750
he's clearly feared by the kids in the neighborhood.

00:24:09.830 --> 00:24:13.066
He doesn't dress up, but he does give his dog a costume, and he does put his

00:24:13.088 --> 00:24:15.314
own twist on the exchange for Halloween candy.

00:24:15.382 --> 00:24:18.846
The visual design of the character is actually based on John Carpenter, the

00:24:18.868 --> 00:24:22.046
director of the movie Halloween, who has not been shy about the fact that he

00:24:22.068 --> 00:24:24.554
doesn't really care what other filmmakers do with the Michael Myers

00:24:24.602 --> 00:24:27.198
character because he's collecting a paycheck no matter what.

00:24:27.284 --> 00:24:31.006
Because of this attitude, he is paid a visit by the Halloween spirit Sam.

00:24:31.118 --> 00:24:34.306
First he hears his dog barking at someone on the front porch and comes out

00:24:34.328 --> 00:24:37.342
to find that it's now covered with over 30 jack o lanterns.

00:24:37.406 --> 00:24:40.902
He comes back in to see the doggy door to the backyard swinging and his dog

00:24:40.956 --> 00:24:42.482
barking at something up the stairs.

00:24:42.546 --> 00:24:45.654
As he turns on the lights, Sam can briefly be seen running across the landing.

00:24:45.692 --> 00:24:48.818
He follows the sound to his bedroom, where he finds an animatronic

00:24:48.834 --> 00:24:52.346
skeleton hand under his sheet and a jack o lantern resembling Sam in the

00:24:52.368 --> 00:24:55.834
corner suddenly goes up in flames and illuminates text painted on the wall

00:24:55.872 --> 00:24:58.380
and ceiling in red spelling trick or treat, give me something good to eat.

00:24:59.710 --> 00:25:03.386
As he's taking this all in, Sam reaches out from under the bed to cut his

00:25:03.408 --> 00:25:04.762
calf Gage Creed style.

00:25:04.826 --> 00:25:08.734
He looks on in surprise and horror as Sam reveals himself and tilts his head

00:25:08.772 --> 00:25:09.786
like Michael Myers.

00:25:09.898 --> 00:25:13.518
Once Sam has peeled his candy wrapper back to reveal a razor blade, a

00:25:13.524 --> 00:25:16.746
reference to an old urban legend about evil neighbors putting razors inside

00:25:16.788 --> 00:25:18.322
of the Halloween candy they hand out.

00:25:18.376 --> 00:25:21.586
Krieg shoots at him, but misses, blowing up the jack o lantern instead.

00:25:21.688 --> 00:25:23.086
Another Halloween sin.

00:25:23.198 --> 00:25:26.914
Sam disappears, and it's not entirely clear if he's more of a ghost like

00:25:26.952 --> 00:25:28.958
creature or if he just dove out of sight.

00:25:29.054 --> 00:25:32.294
Krieg trips on some loose candy and falls down the stairs, hurting his hands

00:25:32.332 --> 00:25:33.958
on the broken glass now at the bottom.

00:25:34.044 --> 00:25:37.954
As his now tender hands frantically try to unlock the front door, Sam sneaks up,

00:25:38.002 --> 00:25:41.786
crawling along the ceiling behind him and ambushes him from above.

00:25:41.808 --> 00:25:44.246
The wall crawling technique is something we've dealt with a lot in Horror History

00:25:44.278 --> 00:25:47.546
when discussing various demons, from The Conjuring's Malthus to

00:25:47.568 --> 00:25:50.346
Insidious' Red Face Demon to Hereditary's Paimon.

00:25:50.448 --> 00:25:53.526
This could suggest that Sam is demonic, though I don't think he's ever

00:25:53.568 --> 00:25:55.022
explicitly referred to as such.

00:25:55.076 --> 00:25:58.666
And as I discussed, most monsters associated with Samhain are Celtic fairies. 

00:25:58.698 --> 00:26:02.478
After a struggle, Sam is thrown into a mirror, and Krieg tries to

00:26:02.484 --> 00:26:03.854
get the attention of his neighbor,

00:26:03.892 --> 00:26:04.830
Mr Wilkins, for help.

00:26:04.900 --> 00:26:08.334
However, he's tackled and choked, so he pulls a move out of Laurie Strode

00:26:08.382 --> 00:26:12.030
from Halloween's playbook by reaching up to remove the mask of his attacker.

00:26:12.110 --> 00:26:15.646
What's revealed underneath is a sinister looking skull resembling a pumpkin

00:26:15.678 --> 00:26:19.106
head with indentations around the eyes and mouth to better resemble a jack o lantern.

00:26:19.128 --> 00:26:22.966
Sam screeches in his face, but Krieg manages to throw him off, so

00:26:22.988 --> 00:26:25.110
he bounces back to feast on the old man's leg.

00:26:25.180 --> 00:26:28.534
However, Krieg also gets a hold of his gun and blasts Sam into the air.

00:26:28.572 --> 00:26:31.634
Across the room, pumpkin guts splattering out on impact.

00:26:31.762 --> 00:26:35.466
No amount of shots, however, are enough to keep him down and prevent his

00:26:35.488 --> 00:26:38.566
severed hand from stabbing Krieg in the foot, like something out of the Evil

00:26:38.598 --> 00:26:39.210
Evil Dead 2.

00:26:39.280 --> 00:26:43.146
When Sam's loose hand finds the rest of his body, he regenerates, puts back

00:26:43.168 --> 00:26:46.782
on his burlap mask, and grabs a new piece of candy from his bag,

00:26:46.836 --> 00:26:50.286
a huge lollipop, which he bites into to create a sharp point on the top.

00:26:50.388 --> 00:26:53.726
He winds up to strike Krieg with it, but when he goes for the kill, his

00:26:53.748 --> 00:26:57.506
tomahawk swing lands in the chocolate bar that Krieg had recovered from one

00:26:57.528 --> 00:26:58.910
of his fleeing trick or treaters.

00:26:58.990 --> 00:27:02.498
By accidentally giving this chocolate bar to Sam, he completes the trick or

00:27:02.504 --> 00:27:05.614
treating transaction, clearly having chosen treats, and the ancient

00:27:05.662 --> 00:27:06.658
tradition is complete.

00:27:06.744 --> 00:27:10.242
So Sam is satisfied and munches down on his candy like a child.

00:27:10.376 --> 00:27:14.374
As he walks away, he looks back at Krieg as if to say, you got lucky this time.

00:27:14.412 --> 00:27:16.598
Don't let me find you breaking the rules again.

00:27:16.684 --> 00:27:19.458
And he seems to have the ability to open and close the door without touching

00:27:19.474 --> 00:27:23.094
it upon his exit, adding to his mysterious set of supernatural abilities.

00:27:23.222 --> 00:27:26.406
When Krieg answers the door for trick or treaters later that night, he's

00:27:26.438 --> 00:27:29.574
wearing bandages from his encounter, which would double as a mummy costume.

00:27:29.622 --> 00:27:32.950
And he's sure to be generous with his candy offerings because he can see Sam

00:27:33.030 --> 00:27:36.410
standing just beyond his yard, making sure that he's celebrating the holiday

00:27:36.490 --> 00:27:37.278
the right way.

00:27:37.364 --> 00:27:40.954
But Sam's night is not over, and he turns his attention to another character

00:27:41.002 --> 00:27:43.066
who's going to violate the rules of Halloween.

00:27:43.178 --> 00:27:46.682
Married couple Emma and Henry return from a night of Halloween festivities,

00:27:46.746 --> 00:27:49.586
and Emma is eager to take down the decorations because her mother is

00:27:49.608 --> 00:27:50.658
visiting the next day.

00:27:50.744 --> 00:27:53.922
Against her husband's warning, she extinguishes the jack o lantern before midnight.

00:27:53.976 --> 00:27:57.410
-[Emma] Why? 
-[Henry] Ancient tradition.

00:27:57.910 --> 00:28:00.138
-[Emma] Henry, it's Halloween, not Hanukkah.

00:28:00.254 --> 00:28:03.442
As she commits this sin, Sam watches from across the street.

00:28:03.506 --> 00:28:06.866
And to make matters worse, she begins taking down the display when Henry

00:28:06.898 --> 00:28:09.270
goes inside and utters the forbidden words.

00:28:09.417 --> 00:28:11.007
– I h*te Halloween.

00:28:11.007 --> 00:28:14.063
Sam hides in the box that she's storing everything in, and when she tosses

00:28:14.095 --> 00:28:17.603
in a white sheet, he explodes on her, drawing screams as he traps her within

00:28:17.625 --> 00:28:20.479
the sheet and slices her throat with his especially sharp Halloween lollipop.

00:28:20.543 --> 00:28:24.423
This scene terrifies a trio of trick or treaters, and he drags her

00:28:24.445 --> 00:28:26.391
back into the yard just as he had dragged the man

00:28:26.429 --> 00:28:30.023
In the original short Season's Greetings. Emma is dismembered, and she

00:28:30.045 --> 00:28:33.447
becomes the scariest part of the yard display that she tried to destroy.

00:28:33.527 --> 00:28:36.891
When Henry comes looking for her, he discovers her head affixed to a post

00:28:36.929 --> 00:28:39.927
with Sam's signature lollipop jammed into her mouth.

00:28:40.007 --> 00:28:41.799
Emma's fate comes as no surprise.

00:28:41.863 --> 00:28:44.955
Not only did she disrespect the holiday, but her extinguishing of the jack o lantern

00:28:44.961 --> 00:28:47.743
breaks an ancient Samhain tradition which would have allowed the

00:28:47.765 --> 00:28:51.007
spirits and monsters to come out and harm her, which turns out to be exactly what happened.

00:28:51.077 --> 00:28:51.871
Perhaps it is Principal Wilkins who said it best

00:28:51.989 --> 00:28:57.715
-[Principal Wilkins] All these traditions jack o lanterns, 

00:28:57.721 --> 00:29:03.283
-[Principal Wilkins] putting on costumes, handing out treats they were started to

00:29:03.305 --> 00:29:09.067
-[Principal Wilkins] protect us, but nowadays no one really cares.

00:29:09.167 --> 00:29:13.959
But Sam's holiday traditions, surprisingly, are not limited to just

00:29:14.013 --> 00:29:14.857
one day a year.

00:29:14.857 --> 00:29:17.801
(Impact)

00:29:19.583 --> 00:29:23.429
🎵Mysterious Music🎵 

00:29:23.567 --> 00:29:27.111
It's presumably a different Halloween when a young child attempts to craft

00:29:27.159 --> 00:29:31.003
himself a Frankensteinian friend using human body parts, candy corn and

00:29:31.025 --> 00:29:31.879
chocolate syrup.

00:29:31.943 --> 00:29:35.483
Sam lends a helping hand by supplying the kid with an abnormal brain, which

00:29:35.505 --> 00:29:39.211
is the last ingredient before electricity that is, to bring this monstrosity

00:29:39.259 --> 00:29:39.759
to life.

00:29:39.797 --> 00:29:43.023
It appears he also takes part in some trick or treating of his own during the day.

00:29:43.045 --> 00:29:47.235
This is from one of ten ads for the trick or treat marathon in 2012.

00:29:47.321 --> 00:29:50.291
There are another four of these that take place on Halloween, each one

00:29:50.329 --> 00:29:52.787
highlighting one Halloween rule using this girl.

00:29:52.857 --> 00:29:56.531
They include wear a costume which doesn't directly feature Sam, but is

00:29:56.569 --> 00:29:58.479
probably the aftermath of one of his attacks.

00:29:58.543 --> 00:30:00.891
Always pass out treats self explanatory.

00:30:00.959 --> 00:30:04.323
Never blow out a jack o lantern, where Sam is presumably the one dragging

00:30:04.355 --> 00:30:05.495
this vandal off screen.

00:30:05.581 --> 00:30:08.855
And always check your candy, where Sam can actually be seen hiding in the

00:30:08.861 --> 00:30:10.227
reflection of this mirror.

00:30:10.307 --> 00:30:13.751
Mike Dougherty is also known for making the Christmas horror movie Krampus,

00:30:13.799 --> 00:30:17.623
which focuses on strict Alpine traditions and legends, so obviously he knows

00:30:17.655 --> 00:30:20.807
a thing or two about other holidays and their origins and customs.

00:30:20.887 --> 00:30:23.591
The rest of the shorts take place on other holidays and milestones

00:30:23.639 --> 00:30:25.335
throughout the year leading up to Halloween.

00:30:25.431 --> 00:30:28.847
The day after shows the mess left behind on the morning of November 1st,

00:30:28.917 --> 00:30:32.283
ending with a pumpkin seed magically planting itself in the soil, which ties

00:30:32.315 --> 00:30:35.135
into the idea of a cycle of life and death that was part of the reason for

00:30:35.141 --> 00:30:37.475
the beginning of the Samhain celebration in the first place.

00:30:37.561 --> 00:30:41.059
It also retroactively connects nicely with Seed, the first trick or treat comic, chronologically. 

00:30:41.113 --> 00:30:44.643
Snowmen takes place in what I'm assuming is

00:30:44.665 --> 00:30:47.875
December, based on the Christmas music, where a bundled up Sam helps a

00:30:47.881 --> 00:30:50.415
little girl bury her dad alive inside of a snowman.

00:30:50.511 --> 00:30:54.003
It's not clear if this man broke some kind of Christmas tradition or if Sam

00:30:54.035 --> 00:30:56.663
is still just getting back at people for the sins that they committed on Halloween,

00:30:56.685 --> 00:31:00.243
but what is clear is he's probably not the first one to suffer

00:31:00.275 --> 00:31:00.835
this fate.

00:31:00.931 --> 00:31:04.635
Easter Candy features Sam in a pair of bunny ears, seemingly orchestrating a

00:31:04.641 --> 00:31:07.335
series of horrific events at this family's Easter brunch.

00:31:07.431 --> 00:31:08.935
Or maybe just spectating.

00:31:09.031 --> 00:31:12.207
Father's Day is the wholesome celebration of fatherhood.

00:31:12.207 --> 00:31:17.215
-[Dad] To the best dad, best dad in the world. 

00:31:19.107 --> 00:31:22.495
This schizo middle aged man sets up this whole scenario where he has a

00:31:22.501 --> 00:31:23.503
family that cares about him using a series of mannequins on strings.

00:31:23.525 --> 00:31:27.199
Sam, the nice guy that he is,

00:31:27.253 --> 00:31:30.463
offers a shrunken head stitched like a baseball, and the two play catch.

00:31:30.575 --> 00:31:33.635
Finally, the last short of the calendar year before coming back around to

00:31:33.641 --> 00:31:37.071
Halloween is called Back to School, which shows Sam packing up various

00:31:37.119 --> 00:31:39.411
things like his razor blade candy bar from the old

00:31:39.449 --> 00:31:40.383
Mr. Krieg segment of Trick r Treat,

00:31:40.415 --> 00:31:43.623
the shrunken head baseball and glove from Father's Day and his

00:31:43.645 --> 00:31:47.095
signature lollipop into a Dead Man's Bones themed lunchbox, which he puts in

00:31:47.101 --> 00:31:49.975
his burlap sack and wears it like a backpack at the bus stop.

00:31:50.061 --> 00:31:53.555
Although he seems friendly to them at first, they eventually end up piled

00:31:53.571 --> 00:31:56.523
inside of his bag, just like the man that tried to cross him all the way

00:31:56.545 --> 00:31:59.559
back in the first short he ever appeared in Seasons Greetings.

00:31:59.623 --> 00:32:02.603
We don't know what these kids transgressions were though, each of these

00:32:02.625 --> 00:32:05.231
shorts serve to tide us over throughout the rest of the year until Halloween.

00:32:05.269 --> 00:32:09.099
But in a way, they serve a similar purpose for Trick r Treat fans

00:32:09.163 --> 00:32:12.507
tidying them over until Trick r Treat can finally get a sequel.

00:32:12.587 --> 00:32:16.899
The future of Sam is uncertain, but in an interview at Beyond Fest in 2022,

00:32:16.953 --> 00:32:21.731
Michael Dougherty revealed this

00:32:21.769 --> 00:32:24.707
-[Interviewer] I am going to ask a question that I'm sure you're all wondering, a sequel?

00:32:26.667 --> 00:32:28.647
-[Mike Dougherty] I'm very excited about the possibility.

00:32:29.067 --> 00:32:31.447
-[Mike Dougherty] Legendary is very excited about the possibility.

00:32:33.067 --> 00:32:36.727
-[Mike Dougherty] It is currently in active development.

00:32:40.267 --> 00:32:42.643
-[Mike Dougherty] That does not mean green lit.

00:32:42.755 --> 00:32:44.807
-[Mike Dougherty] It is an active development.

00:32:45.627 --> 00:32:46.887
-[Mike Dougherty] Very active.

00:32:48.287 --> 00:32:54.859
-[Mike Dougherty] And I hope that we'll be able to share some more news about that soon.

00:32:54.993 --> 00:32:58.335
If and when that day comes, you can be sure I'll be updating this video with

00:32:58.341 --> 00:33:00.187
my complete analysis of Sam.

00:33:00.267 --> 00:33:04.075
So if you love Halloween and love horror, make sure you subscribe to

00:33:04.091 --> 00:33:05.679
CZsWorld for new horrors every week.

00:33:05.733 --> 00:33:09.759
Ring the Deathbell for all notifications, and I will see you in the next one,

00:33:09.813 --> 00:33:12.107
assuming we both survive.

